On Fri, Mar 16, 2012 at 8:34 PM, Bob LeChevalier, President and Founder -
LLG <lojbab@lojban.org> wrote:

> MorphemeAddict wrote:
>
>> That discussion mentions LCOC entries for Lojban:
>> "Searching "Lojban" at the Library of Congress Online Catalog returns
>> basically four records for works in Lojban: (1) /Lojbo karni/ by the LLG,
>> (2) /Ju'i Lobypli/ by R. LeChevalier, (3) /Hoi Loglypli/ by R. LeChevalier,
>> (4) /Me la Uacintyn Loglytuan./ by R. LeChevalier."
>>
>>
>> Are all four of these entries in Lojban? It seems to me that only the
>> first two are. "logl-", "hoi", "tua(n)" smack of TLI Loglan.
>>
>
> All four of those are names for issues of the LLG journal/newletter. The
> first couple of issues were under title (4), and the title is in TLI
> Loglan, since this was 1986-1987.  The third issue was per title (3), again
> in TLI Loglan since it was 1987.  Starting with issue 4 in 1988, the
> journal used title (2) which is in Lojban.  Publication continued until
> 1993, by which time I was juggling too many Lojbanic balls while newly
> parenting 2 kids.  Starting with issue #8, we took the short "news" portion
> of the journal, and published it separately as le lojbo karni - title (1).
>  Something like 120 people got the journal and 400-500 or so got the much
> shorter newsletter.
>
> You can download all of the issues unformatted from
> http://www.lojban.org/files/**jl/ <http://www.lojban.org/files/jl/>
>
> At one point, I had a contact at the LoC who was interested in Lojban, and
> who collected the issues I sent for submittal to the library.  When I found
> out, I supplied him with all the missing issues.
>
> More recently, I believe that copies of our two books were submitted to
> the LoC, so I don't know why they don't show up.
>
> lojbab
> --
> Bob LeChevalier    lojbab@lojban.org    www.lojban.org
